https://github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc/commit/c245815e75e2a5fd60b4290f12bfc04e55a984d3

Reference files:
- internal/xiaomi/xiaomi.go: account/region, device discovery and MISS provisioning
- pkg/xiaomi/cloud.go: Xiaomi account login and RC4 cloud signing
- pkg/xiaomi/crypto/crypto.go: NaCl precomputed session key and ChaCha20 framing
- pkg/xiaomi/miss/client.go: MISS authentication, command and media formats
- pkg/xiaomi/miss/cs2/conn.go: LAN discovery, TCP framing, DRW sequencing and ACKs
- pkg/xiaomi/miss/producer.go: video codec identifiers and timestamp interpretation

The media muxer, Home Assistant integration, lifecycle code, diagnostics
and offline structural tests are supplied as part of this project. go2rtc itself is not bundled
or executed. No Xiaomi native SDK is bundled.

Cryptographic vector references:
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7748
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8439
https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6229
https://nacl.cr.yp.to/box.html

Pan/tilt protocol reference (operation 1=left, 2=right, 3=up, 4=down):
https://github.com/AlexxIT/go2rtc/pull/2531
The encrypted MISS 0x112 motor command and the need to reuse a live camera
session are documented there, with a physical test on chuangmi.camera.029a02.
The Python controls and HA button entities are part of this project.
No ONVIF server or go2rtc runtime is included.

The October 2026 physical Python-implementation PTZ checks are documented
in docs/PTZ_HARDWARE_VERIFICATION_2026-10-24.md in this repository.
The upstream go2rtc result remains a protocol reference only.
